      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "2-Amino-5-tert-butyl-2-oxazoline (ATBO, 2) was synthetized from 3,3-dimethyl-2-iodobutyl isocyanate via N-(3,3-dimethyl-2-iodobutyl) urea (1). The structures of compounds 1 and 2 are based on analytical and spectroscopic data. Compound 2 induced in rats and mice a peripheral antinociceptive effect through both spinal and supraspinal mechanisms. ATBO did not impair motor coordination or activity of the experimental animals."},
